Product Requirements Document
1. Problem & Context
Guests begin their journey on the airbnb.co.in homepage using the unified search bar (Where, dates,
guests). We need consistent routing from the homepage directly to the results page with all user inputs
preserved. Additionally, guests require immediate access to filters and the map so they can refine their
search and make quick decisions. This aligns with documented Airbnb search behavior and refinement
workflows.
2. Core User Story
As a guest starting on the airbnb.co.in homepage,
I want to enter a destination, optional dates, and guests, and land on a results page that reflects
those inputs,
so I can refine my search using filters and a map to find a place that fits my trip.
(Note: "Search results page" explicitly means the user typed a destination city in the 'Where' field on the
homepage and clicked Search, regardless of whether dates were provided).
3. Goals & Non-Goals
Goals
Route users successfully from the homepage search to the Homes results page with destination,
dates, and guests preserved.
Ensure the results page supports continuous refinement via Filters and Map controls.
Keep the entered inputs visible and editable directly on the results page to prevent users from having
to use the browser's "back" button to adjust their query.
Non-Goals
Changes to the checkout flow or pricing logic.
Modifications to the underlying search ranking or recommendation algorithms.
Mobile application (iOS/Android) feature parity (this initiative is strictly Web).
Feature: Homepage Search to Homes Results Routing & Refinement
Platform: Web Desktop / Mobile Web (airbnb.co.in)
Target Audience: Guests searching for Homes
