4. Scope Definitions
In-Scope
Homepage Search Bar: Displays fields for Where , Check-in , Check-out , and Who . Accepts typed
destinations (city/region), optional dates, and guest counts.
Routing & Display: On clicking Search, the Homes results page opens. Applied parameters must be
visible in the results header.
Refinement Tools: The results page exposes existing Filters and Map controls.
Flow 1: Complete Input: Search with destination, valid check-in/checkout dates, and guests.
Flow 2: Partial Input: Search with destination and guests only (no dates). Results load for the
destination, allowing the user to add dates directly on the results page later.
Localization (i18n): Maintain existing English (IN) labels visible on the homepage and results pages.
Out-of-Scope
Introduction of new filter types or the reordering of existing filters.
Routing or results configuration for Experiences/Services (handled in separate stories).
Any structural or visual changes to the global header navigation.
